    {
      "turn": 1,
      "user": "I'm in Seattle. Will the city approve my hempcrete walls under Appendix BL?",
      "assistant": "In Seattle, whether your hempcrete walls can be approved under the 2024 International Residential Code Appendix BL depends entirely on the local adoption timeline and the discretion of the Seattle Department of Construction and Inspections (SDCI). While Appendix BL provides a model-code framework for hemp-lime construction, model codes are not automatically active until formally adopted by the local jurisdiction or accepted via an alternative materials and methods request. \n\nBecause hemp-lime acts as a non-load-bearing infill requiring a conventional structural frame (like timber framing) to carry loads, you will need to work closely with a qualified local professional to submit your specific project design for review.\n\nWould you like to calculate the total hemp-lime volume needed for your wall area and thickness so you can discuss the material scope with your designer?",
